oundex algorithm placement \u2014 `OwnerIdentity` is accreting a general string algorithm.** `OwnerIdentity` is documented narrowly as \"Single source of truth for an owner's identityKey,\" but now also hosts a ~45-line general-purpose American Soundex implementation (`soundex` + `charCode`), which `FlagPossibleDuplicate` reaches into purely for last-name similarity matching \u2014 a household/name-matching concern, not identity-key construction. The codebase's own idiom is to give a reusable, self-contained rule its own focused helper (`OwnerTelephones` for phone normalization, `HouseholdKey` for the household definition). Soundex fits that mold and would be more natural as its own helper (e.g. `Soundex`, or folded into the household/name-key helper), with both `OwnerIdentity` and `FlagPossibleDuplicate` depending on it directly. As written, `OwnerIdentity` is becoming a catch-all for \"all string-normalization used anywhere near identity,\" and `FlagPossibleDuplicate`'s dependency on it for name matching reads as borrowing rather than a genuine identity-key use.\n\nNeither is a correctness concern \u2014 both are about putting the logic in the right unit and not duplicating the hashing step the codebase already single-sources."
